% Scenario: a 300 dpi gray image at 72. A 300x300-sample 8-bit gray
% gradient (each row the same ramp from 0 to 255) drawn one inch square
% is 300 samples per inch; with DownsampleGrayImages true and
% GrayImageResolution 72 the written image is 75x75 samples, each the
% rounded average of a 4x4 block, and the page renders the same within
% tolerance.
<< /DownsampleGrayImages true /GrayImageResolution 72 >> setdistillerparams
/row 300 string def
0 1 299 { dup 255 mul 299 idiv row 3 1 roll put } for
72 648 translate
72 72 scale
300 300 8 [300 0 0 -300 0 300] { row } image
showpage
